is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router_core_3
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the host-based firewall on router_core_3 (iptables). Traffic from both pods to the server farm (10.200.0.0/24) must traverse router_core_3: on router_core_1 the route to 10.200.0.0/24 points to 172.16.0.3 (core_3 eth0), and on router_core_2 it points to 172.16.0.5 (core_3 eth1). On router_core_3 we found an explicit FORWARD-chain drop: “-A FORWARD -d 10.200.0.0/24 -j DROP” with counters showing hits (44 packets/3696 bytes). This explains why pod-to-pod traffic is unaffected (not destined to 10.200.0.0/24), why router_core_3 itself can ping 10.200.0.2 (local OUTPUT chain, not FORWARD), and why switch_server_access and servers can talk among themselves (same L2 segment, no forwarding). 
